    </content>
    <glossary>
    <definition id="def-00001">
    <term>abstinence-only education</term>
    <meaning>teaches that abstaining from sex is expected until marriage; this educational track typically excludes information about the utility of contraception and condoms to prevent pregnancy and STIs</meaning>
    </definition>
    <definition id="def-00002">
    <term>abstinence-plus education</term>
    <meaning>promotes abstinence but includes information about contraception and condoms</meaning>
    </definition>
    <definition id="def-00003">
    <term>comprehensive sex education</term>
    <meaning>offers medically accurate, age-appropriate information about development, sexual behavior (including abstinence), healthy relationships, life and communication skills, sexual orientation, and gender identity</meaning>
    </definition>
    <definition id="def-00004">
    <term>sex positivity</term>
    <meaning>approach to adolescent sexuality that encourages exploration and experimentation within safe and openly discussed parameters</meaning>
    </definition>
    <definition id="def-00005">
    <term>sexually transmitted disease (STD)</term>
    <meaning>refers to STI that has led to some symptom of disease</meaning>
    </definition>
    <definition id="def-00006">
    <term>sexually transmitted infection (STI)</term>
    <meaning>infection transmitted through sexual contact, caused by bacteria, viruses, or parasites</meaning>
    </definition>
    </glossary>
    </document>